    "summary": "High‑energy April ’82 with stellar China Cat > Rider and electric Deep Elem",
    "blurb": "The show bursts into life with a blazing China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue and an electrifying Deep Elem Blues. Playin' In The Band drives the second set, while Jack Straw and Bertha showcase tight group interplay. A crisp soundboard capture makes this performance especially rewarding.",
    "review": "What unfolds at Glenns Falls Civic Center on April 14‑82 is a high‑octane snapshot of the Dead in full stride. The first set starts unevenly but quickly finds its groove, highlighted by Jerry’s gritty vocal on Big River and an electric Deep Elem Blues that many reviewers call “masterful.” The second set lifts off with a seamless China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider transition that feels both tight and exploratory, leading into a soaring Playin' In The Band that rides Brent’s sparkling keyboards and Bob’s slide‑laden Bertha. Drums and Space build tension before the band rolls through The Wheel, I Need A Miracle, and a rousing Black Peter, culminating in a second, even more intense Playin' In The Band and a classic Johnny B. Goode encore. Across recordings the soundboard version stands out for its crisp mix and articulation, though some listeners note vocals pushed forward; matrix tapes suffer from time‑delay artifacts, while several audience tapes capture the raw energy with surprising clarity. Overall, this show delivers the quintessential 1982 Dead experience—electric, adventurous, and richly textured.",
